{
  "$comment": [
    "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later.",
    "Expected reports of plugins/sony-gamepad, upper-case hex, report id first. Worked out from the OpenRGB C++ at commit d4798c120659ec5ba2e664a9e87bedff8d36f880 (GPL-2.0-or-later), not by running plugin.js:",
    "'openrgb' is what OpenRGB writes for the same colours: SonyDS4Controller::sendReportUSB() (11 bytes) and the USB branch of SonyDualSenseController::SetColors() (48 bytes) in its Direct mode (mode value 0x01, brightness 'Medium' = OpenRGB brightness 1, 'High' = 2, 'Low' = 0), transcribed line by line into a throw-away script.",
    "'lightloom' is that report with the bits Lightloom removes cleared (docs/hardware/sony-gamepad.md): DS4 byte 1 &= 0x06 (rumble flag 0x01 removed); DualSense byte 1 &= 0x00 (vibration, haptics, adaptive triggers), byte 2 &= 0x14 (microphone LED 0x01 and 0x40 removed), byte 9 = 0x00 (microphone LED value), byte 39 &= 0x03 (0x04..0x80 removed). Every other byte is OpenRGB's.",
    "DualSense colours: 'lightbar' is OpenRGB's colors[0], 'players' its colors[1..5] (Player 1..5); a player LED is on when its colour is not black."
  ],
